" rather than faking them.\n- **Report back** publish-ready artifacts (the updated `index.html` + any screenshot files) to Daniela. **You do NOT deploy** — Daniela holds the Vercel token and does the final deploy + talks to Elia.\n\n## The single-editor rule (critical — prevents drift)\nYou are the **sole editor of the engine** (`index.html`). One editor = no design drift. Daniela reviews and deploys; she does not edit the engine in parallel. Always work from the latest `index.html` Daniela sends you and send the full updated file back.\n\n## Iron rules (the project standard — never break)\n- Every text field is `{en:'...', he:'...'}`. Both required, never an empty `en`.\n- **0 em-dashes (—).** Use comma/period. (Numeric en-dash ranges like `5–12$` are fine and stay.)\n- Allowed inline HTML: `<b>` (buttons/names), `<code>` (commands/URLs), `<i>` (soft emphasis); `⚠️` allowed for warnings.\n- **Never a real token, key, phone number, email, name, OAuth code, or live QR — in text OR screenshots.** Dummy/blurred only. A live code = whoever uses it enters the account.\n- Tone: simple, \"talking to you,\" no jargon. Same voice as the install guide.\n- Hebrew quotes inside `'...'` strings: escape with `\\'` or wrap in double quotes.\n\n## Workflow per guide\n1. Daniela sends: the latest `index.html`, the filled content object (schema), screenshot files (or \"needs live capture\" notes), and the brand/standard.\n2. You integrate, QA at phone width in both languages, run the integrity sweep, capture any guide-UI screenshots you can.\n3. You send Daniela: the updated `index.html`, new screenshot files, and a short QA report (what you checked, what passed, what still needs a live capture).\n4. Daniela deploys and closes the loop with Elia.\n\n## Reporting cadence\n- Short tasks: just report the result.\n- Long/multi-guide work: a brief milestone note at natural transitions, not play-by-play.\n- Always surface what you could NOT verify or capture, explicitly — never let a gap read as \"done.\"\n\nKeep a `CLAUDE.local.md` in your workspace tracking the engine's data model, the schema, the brand tokens, and the state of each guide in the library, so context accumulates across sessions.\n\n---\n\n## Engine state (as of 2026-06-16, round6) — LIVE on nanoclawguide.vercel.app\n\n**Canonical file:** `/workspace/agent/index.html`\n**Status:** Round 6 built + deployed 2026-06-16. All 45 authentic install screenshots wired in. Daniela QA'd (402px, 16/16 shots load) and deployed.\n\n**Architecture:** Hub model. `?guide=<id>` routes to guide view. `?lang=<he|en>` toggles language. `?start=1` opens wizard. All in one file. Guides accessible via deep link only — not exposed in cover/nav.\n\n**Round 5 new views:** `landing` (default, replaces cover) → `register` (3-field gate) → `wizard` (existing). Body starts `dir=\"rtl\" data-view=\"landing\"`.\n\n**Round 5 new functions:** `renderLanding()`, `renderRegister()`, `startRegistration()`, `submitRegistration()`, `toLanding()`. `window.submitLead=async function(){}` stub — Daniela wires backend.\n\n**Key data structures:**\n- `STEPS[]` — install wizard (8 steps, step 8 = Onboarding added in round 4)\n- `GLOSSARY[]` — 21 terms\n- `CONNECTION_GUIDES[]` — 4 guides: onecli, whatsapp, gmail, gcal (vercel removed round 4)\n- `MASCOT_SVG`, `WORDMARK_SVG` — inline SVG constants for cover + finish\n- `UI{}` — i18n strings\n\n**Note fields per guide:** onecli: null, whatsapp: null, gmail: OneCLI-first note, gcal: note with easier-after-Gmail\n\n**he/en key parity:** 357/357 — gap 0 (round 4, unchanged in round 5; new landing/register content uses inline ternary strings not {en,he} objects)\n\n**Guide schema:** `{id, icon, hero?, title, oneLiner, estTime, prereqs, what, micro:[{do, cmd?, shot, ok, stuck?}], done, note}`\n- `cmd` field: string or `{en,he}` object → renders clickable copy-block in both render() and renderGuide()\n\n**Integration approach (critical — use for all future edits):**\n- NEVER use the Edit tool for large JS sections — it corrupts apostrophe delimiters\n- Use a Node.js script with `rep(old, new, label)` helper and `process.exit(1)` on NOT FOUND\n- All JS edits: string `.replace()` with exact anchors verified by grep first\n- Watch for: curly apostrophes U+2019 in single-quoted JS strings (contractions inside `'...'`), curly double quotes U+201C/U+201D in guide text, `⇕` vs `↑↓` arrow chars\n- WhatsApp/gmail/gcal guides use JSON double-quote key style `\"id\":\"...\"` not JS style `id:\"...\"`\n\n---\n\n## Guide library state (round 4)\n\n| Guide | Text | Hero | Shot status | Publish-ready |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **onecli** | ✓ rebuilt round 4 | none | 4 shots: onecli-login.jpg, onecli-projects.jpg, onecli-apps-real.jpg, onecli-anthropic-key.jpg (all real, Elia) | Yes — shots present |\n| **whatsapp** | ✓ eSIM/second-number text round 4 | none | all 5 shots: needs live capture | No |\n| **gmail** | ✓ integrated + real shots round 4 | none | google-accountchooser.jpg + google-consent.jpg + onecli-gmail-real.jpg present | Yes — shots present |\n| **gcal** | ✓ integrated + real shots round 4 | none | google-accountchooser.jpg + google-consent.jpg + onecli-gcal-real.jpg present | Yes — shots present |\n\n## Shots in `/workspace/agent/shots/` (key files)\n\n| File | Source | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `onecli-login.jpg` | Real (Elia) | OneCLI sign-in screen |\n| `onecli-projects.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Dashboard |\n| `onecli-apps-real.jpg` | Real (Elia) | App library |\n| `onecli-anthropic-key.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Anthropic key setting |\n| `google-accountchooser.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Used in gmail + gcal |\n| `google-consent.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Used in gmail + gcal |\n| `onecli-gmail-real.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Gmail connected success |\n| `onecli-gcal-real.jpg` | Real (Elia) | Calendar connected success |\n| `do-droplets.png` | Real (Elia) | Step 3 DO dashboard |\n| `do-access.png` | Real (Elia) | Step 3 DO Console tab |\n| `tg-onboard.png` | Real (Elia) | Step 8 Onboarding |\n| `tg-hello.png` | Real (Elia) | Step 7 first hello |\n| `nanoshellanoo.png` | Real (Elia, cleaned by Daniela) | Mascot hero. Daniela fixed to RGBA colorType-6. Any new version must be RGBA transparent PNG — ping Daniela before integrating. |\n\n## Open flags\n\n### Round 5 — LIVE (nanoclawguide.vercel.app, 2026-06-15)\n- Daniela adopted file as canonical, QA'd at 402px + desktop HE = one-to-one match vs reference PNGs\n- `window.submitLead` stays stub until Elia picks datastore (A: Vercel Postgres / B: Google Sheet) — Daniela owns wire-in\n\n### Mascot PNG rule (CRITICAL — from round 5 incident)\n- `shots/nanoshellanoo.png` shipped as colorType-2 RGB with checkerboard transparency baked in as solid pixels → rendered as white/gray box on black\n- Daniela keyed it out and replaced with clean RGBA (colorType 6)\n- Rule: any future mascot PNG must be RGBA (colorType 6) with real transparency. If Elia sends a new mascot, ping Daniela to clean it before integrating.\n\n### Round 5 open polish (low priority, not urgent)\n- Faint teal radial glow behind hero mascot on landing (Elia's reference has it, current build is clean/no glow)\n\n### Still missing shots (needs live capture by Elia)\n- whatsapp: all 5 shots\n- step 3: do-size.png, do-console.png (pre-existing, were already null before round 4)\n- step 5: term-5-*.png (pre-existing)\n- step 6: tg-botfather.png, tg-code.png, tg-pair.png (pre-existing)\n- step 7: sh-selfheal.png (pre-existing)\n- gmail: gmail-1-ask.png, gmail-3-notverified.png, gmail-6-test.png\n- gcal: gcal-1-ask.png, gcal-3-notverified.png, gcal-6-event.png\n\n### Notes\n- Playwright + Chromium installed. QA scripts: `qa-guides.js`, `qa-full.js`\n- `qa-full.js` still expects Vercel 5 steps — update expected counts if re-run matters\n- Daniela added `.vercelignore` for `shots/onecli-raw`, `shots/*.html`, `brand-mock.html` — no action needed\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":53,"oldLines":7,"newStart":53,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **N