hort HERE (don't over-explain).\n40\t- The real emphasis = put in the OPENING NARRATIVE (beginning of guide): this guide is 100% NOT for technical people. Because we're non-technical it takes ~30–40 min; only ~5 of those minutes are hands-on actions we do without being technical. More technical people will be faster — but we walk WITH you step by step.\n41\t- Action: keep the time chip on micro-4; weave the non-technical/time reassurance into the step-1 opener narrative (the \"מכאן זה נהיה מעשי...\" / tone bridge area).\n42\t\n43\t## Screen: Step 1 main page — ADD A מקרא / LEGEND (#2228) [BIG one]\n44\t- He wants the MAIN page to carry a **מקרא (legend)** that explains how the guide works + all the visual conventions, so the whole process feels easy from the start. Explain each marker:\n45\t  1. **🔵 כחול / קוד** = the things to **copy-paste** (commands/code). Inside a box; one tap copies it.\n46\t  2. **🔗 קישורים** = links that take you to the sites where you download / do actions.\n47\t  3. **📷 צילומי מסך** = real screenshots of the exact screens you'll go through (very easy/accessible).\n48\t  4. **🔴 אדום = \"נתקעת?\"** = if you hit a problem, the box states your problem + exactly how to solve it.\n49\t- Also explain NAVIGATION on this page:\n50\t  - **תפריט ימני (rail)** = the steps we'll go through.\n51\t  - **חלק תחתון** = the connections (חיבורים נוספים) you can add.\n52\t- Tone/goal: page PREPARES you for the whole guide + full overview, and ABOVE ALL gives confidence: \"עוברים שלב אחרי שלב, אני יד ביד אתכם בכל התהליך.\" Must be very concise and to-the-point despite covering all this.\n53\t### CROSS-CUTTING voice principle (#2230)\n54\t- Weave Elia's PERSONAL first-person presence into the copy: \"ככה אני הולך להוביל אתכם\", \"אני מלווה אתכם\", \"אני איתכם לאורך כל הדרך\". Turns the guide from generic → personal.\n55\t- Especially good on the MAIN page + around the מקרא (\"this is how I'll lead you\").\n56\t- GENTLE + in the right spots only — do NOT break th