 = copy block.\n86\t- Ref: צילום מסך ...334227.jpg (step 6 console — `root` login etc shown as inline chips → make copyable).\n87\t\n88\t## (personal voice, cont.) ##\n89\t- **Concrete narrative to use (#2232):** Elia's personal-voice \"I keep updating this\" line — \"כשאני אראה שבאמת יש עניין, אני אתקן ואשפר את המדריך ואכין לכם את זה שוב. אני אעדכן כל הזמן — תישארו מעודכנים.\" Gives: (a) demand signal (\"אני רואה שיש ביקוש\"), (b) community voice, (c) ties directly to the SOFT-REGISTER (name+email, weekly updates) on Screen 2 — same thread, his voice. Use this narrative as one of the tasteful personal touch-points.\n90\t\n91\t## Screen: Step 3 DigitalOcean — REMOVE the redundant BOTTOM link card (#2246)\n92\t- Ref: attachment-1781596432632.jpg (bottom of step-3: a big \"פתח את DigitalOcean ↖\" button card sitting at the very bottom, AFTER all the content + after the inline \"פתח את DigitalOcean / digitalocean.com\" link + the 4GB/not-Google-Cloud note).\n93\t- Elia: \"אני לא רואה צורך לשים למטה את הפתח הזה. נורא נורא מיותר. הרי אנחנו שמים לינקים בכל מקום, ואנחנו מתחילים את המדריך תמיד בלשים את הלינק. אז מה חוכמה? בנינו את הכל ובסוף שמים למטה. זה מיותר. אין צורך.\"\n94\t- Action: DELETE the trailing big \"open <provider>\" CTA card that sits at the bottom of a step. The link to the provider/service already appears AT THE TOP / at the moment the step opens (each step starts by placing its link), and links are sprinkled inline throughout → a duplicate link button at the very bottom adds nothing.\n95\t- GENERALIZE: audit all internal steps for an end-of-page \"open X\" button that merely repeats the link already given at the step's start → remove those. Keep the link where the action happens (top/inline), not as a tail.\n96\t- CLARIFY (#2256): the CARD STYLE itself is fine (\"אולי גם ככה בצורה הזאת\") — the problem is POSITION. The \"פתח את X\" card belongs at the TOP of the step (you open the service FIRST, then follow the steps), NOT at the bottom after you've already read everything. Rationale: \"אני עובר על כל המדריך ובסוף את שולחת אותי לפתוח אנטרופיק — אין לזה הגיון.\" → MOVE the open-service card to the top of each step (or remove if a top link already exists); never leave it as the tail.\n97\t\n98\t- Build note: a compact legend card (4 marker rows + a short nav line). Verify against engine — confirm blue is used for copy-paste code vs links (avoid blue meaning two things; align legend to actual tokens). There's already a LOCAL terminal legend in step 5 (📋/📷/↑↓) — this is the GLOBAL one on the main page; keep them consistent, don't duplicate confusingly.\n99\t\n100\t## Screen: Step 7 \"תגיד שלום\" — warmer personal title + emoji policy (#2270)\n101\t- Ref: attachment-1781597659182.jpg (step 7 title \"תגיד שלום 👋\", still showing the old chips).\n102\t- TITLE: make it warmer/personal → **\"תגיד שלום לננוקלו שלך\"** (say hello to YOUR NanoClaw). He liked that phrasing, \"היה לי יותר חם, לא סתם תגיד שלום.\"\n103\t- (Chips still visible here = same #2268 removal applies; this is the live screen not my updated sample.)\n104\t\n105\t## Screen: Step 8 rename + the \"שלנו vs שלך\" naming strategy (#2274)\n106\t- Ref: attachment-1781597783630.jpg (step 8 currently \"היכרות ראשונה\").\n107\t- Step 8 title → **\"היכרות עם הסוכן שלך\"** (NOT \"היכרות ראשונה\"). Pairs with step 7 \"תגיד שלום לננוקלו שלך\".\n108\t- STRATEGY (lock this as a naming principle): the GUIDE/brand is **\"NanoShellano שלנו\"** (ours — for everyone, inclusive). At the PERSONAL agent moments (steps 7-8, the talk-to-your-agent beats) flip to **\"שלך\"** (yours) — \"הנה הננוקלו שלך\". Deliberate play: brand = שלנו/לכולם; the agent itself = שלך/אישי. Aligns the talk-to-the-agent strategy with the brand voice. Apply \"שלך\" at the personal touchpoints, \"שלנו\" for the guide/brand framing.\n109\t\n110\t## GLOBAL: EMOJI POLICY — Elia prefers NONE; be consistent (#2270)\n111\t- Elia: doesn't like the 👋 emoji. \"או שאנחנו הולכים עם כל הסמלים אמוג'י או בלי. אני פשוט פחות אוהב אמוג'י.\" → pick ONE consistent policy; his lean = NO emojis.\n112\t- DECISION (proposing): remove decorative emojis from step TITLES + headings + prose (👋, ☕ etc.) for a cleaner, more grown-up look.\n113\t- The LEGEND/markers (🔵🔗📷🔴) + 💡 tip: replace emoji with clean on-brand glyphs/shapes so the guide stays consistent and not emoji-y — e.g. small colored DOTS / SVG icons (teal/blue/red), word \"טיפ\" with a teal bar instead of 💡. Keeps the functional meaning without the emoji aesthetic. (Confirm scope with Elia: internal screens now; the external persona screen's role icons are emoji too — decide whether the no-emoji rule extends there or those stay as role icons.)\n114\t- Apply consistently across the whole guide once confirmed.\n115\t\n116\t## GLOBAL: REMOVE status chips + TIGHTEN the step head (#2268)\n117\t- Ref: attachment-1781597349623.jpg (the \"● מוכן\" status pill + \"👤 אתה עושה\" owner tag under the H1).\n118\t- Elia: the chips (\"מוכן\" / \"אתה עושה\") are CONFUSING and unnecessary — \"אני עובר מדריך שלב אחרי שלב, פשוט עושה. לא יודע מה מוכן מה לא, זה מבלבל.\" → REMOVE the status pill + owner tag from every step head. (Drop the `status`/`owner` chip rendering globally.)\n119\t- He likes the clean structure: **כותרת ראשית → כותרת משנה (one-liner) → קצת דגש → פסקת מבוא (\"מה קורה כאן\")**. Add a SUBTITLE/lead one-liner under the H1 (was missing). Done in sample v4: H1 → teal-accent lead line → de-boxed \"מה קורה כאן\" → tip. No chips.\n120\t- TIGHTEN: too much up top + \"יותר מדי הנחיות למטה\" → trim redundancy, lighter feel, fewer directives. Removed the extra duplicate body paragraph (merged into the intro). Keep the head minimal because the micro-steps below already carry many instructions.\n121\t- KEEP (do NOT remove): the \"✦ זה נשמע טכני אבל זה רק העתק-הדבק\" reassurance line — Elia explicitly wants it (\"נותן ביטחון\"). I did NOT remove it from the guide; the type sample is just a different step (2) that doesn't carry it. Confirm it stays on the install/command steps.\n122\t\n123\t## Screen: RAIL bottom — \"request more guides\" feature = 2nd lead source (#2306) [his agent's idea]\n124\t- Add to the BOTTOM of the side rail (under \"חיבורים נוספים\"): a \"which other guides do you want me to build?\" request box. Doubles as (a) another LEAD capture point, (b) a demand signal telling Elia which connections to build next (prioritize by votes), (c) reframes the limited connection set as a feature: \"אלה החיבורים הבסיסיים; רוצה עוד? בקש כאן.\"\n125\t- Interaction: a checkbox/picker panel — \"איזה עוד מדריכים תרצה שאכין?\" → user ticks desired connections from a list (everything OneCLI supports: phone/SMS, HubSpot/CRMs, Slack, Notion, etc.) + an \"אחר (כתוב לי)\" free field.\n126\t- Submit logic (reuses the SAME leads backend): if the user ALREADY registered (we have name+email from the persona register) → one tap sends, no re-ask. If NOT → inline name+email (\"תשאיר שם ומייל ואעדכן אותך כשהמדריך מוכן\"). New lead fields: requestedGuides[] + source='guide-request'.\n127\t- Confirmation tone ties to the weekly-update narrative (\"אעדכן אותך כשהמדריך מוכן\") → same \"I keep building this for you\" thread, non-selling.\n128\t- MY OPINION (agree, with one caution): great idea, lead-gen + roadmap signal in one. CAUTION: don't dump an \"infinite list\" — curate a scannable top-N of the most-wanted connections + \"אחר\", with \"ועוד...\" for the long tail. A wall of 40 integrations = friction; a tight list + free field = inviting.\n129\t- DEPENDENCY: needs the leads backend wired (same Google-Sheet/Vercel store still pending Elia's Apps Script /exec). Build the UI now; wire on submit when the store is live. Same store, just another source tag.\n130\t\n131\t## BUG: shots VANISH on refresh — FALSE ALARM, was the OLD guide (#2296→#2298)\n132\t- RETRACTED by Elia (#2298): he'd accidentally opened an OLD/cached guide → ignore the urgency. Files are fine (all 200 live).\n133\t- KEEP as low-pri hardening for the big build (not urgent, not a separate round): the `loading=\"lazy\"` + destructive `onerror=\"this.parentNode.style.display='none'\"` pattern (index.html lines 1382/1510/1519) IS brittle — fold a hardening (eager load + don't permanently hide an existing shot) into the next big round. Not standalone.\n134\t- Symptom (for reference): Elia saw all his screenshots, refreshed, they DISAPPEARED.\n135\t- DIAGNOSIS (done): the FILES are fine — every shot returns 200 on nanoclawguide.vercel.app (verified do-product/term-key-entered/sh-delivered/tg-paircode/term-onecli-found/do-droplet-active all 200; index.html 200). Not a missing-file / .vercelignore problem.\n136\t- ROOT CAUSE: the engine renders shots as `<img ... loading=\"lazy\" onerror=\"this.parentNode.style.display='none'\">`. The `onerror` PERMANENTLY hides the whole shot frame on ANY load failure — including transient ones. On a hard refresh the browser aborts in-flight image requests / a lazy image mid-load errors → onerror fires → the shot is gone until a clean full reload. The lazy+destructive-onerror combo is the footgun. (This onerror was added so gated/placeholder slots degrade gracefully, but it also nukes REAL shots on a momentary glitch.)\n137\t- FIX (builder): make existing shots robust. (a) Drop `loading=\"lazy\"` on in-flow install/guide shots → load eager (matches the \"16/16 eager\" note). (b) Don't let onerror permanently hide a shot that exists: either remove the hide for known-present shots, or retry the src once before hiding, and reserve the graceful-hide ONLY for known placeholder/gated slots (shot:null/'pending'). Goal: a refresh never makes an authentic shot disappear.\n138\t\n139\t## Screen: Connection guides — add each app's LOGO/icon in the header (#2296)\n140\t- Ref: attachment-1781599039959.jpg (Google Calendar connect screen — the title carries a generic ▶ play icon, not the Calendar logo).\n141\t- Elia: add the actual app logo/icon per connection guide (Google Calendar logo, Gmail, WhatsApp, etc.) in the header. Optional but \"עושה את זה יותר מעניין\" — every app shown with its own logo. Use clean brand SVGs/PNGs; non-blocking nicety.\n142\t\n143\t## Screen: WhatsApp — it's a CHAT CHANNEL, belongs UP with Telegram, not in \"חיבורים נוספים\" (#2294)\n144\t- Ref: attachment-1781598910927.jpg (the WhatsApp connect screen — also shows the same fragmentation: \"לפני שמתחילים\" + \"מה קורה כאן\" boxes repeating → apply the #2288 de-fragment fix here too).\n145\t- Elia thinking out loud: WhatsApp + Telegram are the SAME kind of thing (your chat channel to talk to the agent), so doing WhatsApp separately down in \"חיבורים נוספים\" is confusing. He'd rather have a \"connect Telegram / connect WhatsApp\" pairing UP TOP (in the core chat-app step), with Telegram as the easy default. At minimum WhatsApp must sit ABOVE OneCLI (OneCLI is for connecting to \"more stuff\" = a different category).\n146\t- MY RECOMMENDATION (agree + sharpen): WhatsApp is a chat CHANNEL, not a capability integration. So:\n147\t  - Core step 6 (\"חיבור אפליקציית הצ'אט\") = pick your channel: **Telegram (recommended, easiest) OR WhatsApp** — both live here, up top, as the two paths to talk to the agent.\n148\t  - Bottom \"חיבורים נוספים\" = only the capability integrations: OneCLI (vault) → Gmail → Calendar → CRM etc. WhatsApp LEAVES the bottom list entirely.\n149\t  - This is cleaner than \"WhatsApp above OneCLI in the bottom list\" — it puts like with like (channels up, integrations down) and removes the confusion he flagged.\n150\t- SCREENSHOTS: WhatsApp shots are missing — Elia already connected WhatsApp in his agent, so a fresh capture is hard; he'll arrange/organize the shots for me. Until then the WhatsApp path stays a needs-capture placeholder (pairs via QR, vault-exempt). Keep Telegram the fully-shot default so the core flow is never blocked.\n151\t\n152\t## GLOBAL: NAV (back/next) at BOTTOM too, not only top (#2290/#2292)\n153\t- Ref: ...803252.jpg (back arrow \"חזרה\" at the TOP) + ...803315.jpg (bottom of the OneCLI step = \"✓ OneCLI מוכנה\" box + \"נתקעת כאן?\" + page end, NO nav button at the bottom).\n154\t- Elia: convenient to have the back/nav BOTH top AND bottom — after you read to the bottom you shouldn't have to scroll back up to navigate (\"אתה לא מרגיש שאתה צריך לחפש?\"). Asks my opinion.\n155\t- DECISION (agree): standard guide UX → put the prev/next nav at the BOTTOM of every step (where you finish reading), AND keep a quick \"חזרה\" at the top. My type sample already has a bottom `.nav` (prev+next). Apply globally: every internal step ends with back + continue buttons; top keeps a back affordance. No scrolling up to advance.\n156\t\n157\t## Screen: OneCLI step — DE-FRAGMENT + nail the VALUE in one clear shot (#2288)\n158\t- Ref: attachment-1781598647060.jpg (the OneCLI step: title \"אונקלייי: הכספת שלך\" → subtitle → \"3 דקות\" chip → \"לפני שמתחילים\" box → another paragraph → \"מה קורה כאן\" box — ALL saying roughly the same thing, chopped into 4-5 fragments → user still doesn't get what OneCLI IS).\n159\t- Elia: too fragmented; the repetition-across-boxes makes it LESS clear, not more. Same disease as #2262/#2268 (over-boxing/over-fragmenting). Consolidate into ONE crisp value statement.\n160\t- **The ONE value to land (his words):** OneCLI is the SECURE way the agent connects to additional apps/systems. Its value = when you connect to more apps, OneCLI PROTECTS you (sits between the agent and the services, holds your credentials safely). The key thing the user must grasp on this first screen: **connect to OneCLI once → you can then interface NanoClaw with EVERY app/system that has an API — from personal Gmail/calendar to CRM systems and anything else. One connection opens everything, securely.**\n161\t- TITLE fix: drop the Hebrew translit \"אונקלייי\" → \"OneCLI: הכספת שלך\" (per #2286).\n162\t- Action: collapse the fragmented intro into a single clean lead paragraph (no duplicate boxes). Proposed: \"OneCLI היא הכספת המאובטחת של הסוכן. חיבור אחד דרכה, ו-NanoClaw יכול להתממשק לכל אפליקציה ומערכת שיש לה API — מ-Gmail והיומן ועד מערכות CRM וכל דבר אחר. היא שומרת על המפתחות והסיסמאות שלך, כך שהסוכן ניגש לשירותים בלי שתצטרך להחזיק אותם בעצמך, והכל ניתן לביטול בכל רגע.\" Then the \"מה לעשות\" steps. One value para, not 4 fragments.\n163\t- Generalize the lesson: when several blocks on a screen are paraphrasing the same point, MERGE into one — fragmentation reads as confusion.\n164\t\n165\t## Screen: \"חיבורים נוספים\" rail — OneCLI label + WhatsApp-first order (#2286)\n166\t- **Drop the Hebrew transliteration \"אונקליי\"** — unclear what it is. Keep \"OneCLI\" in Latin and label it by what it DOES: \"חיבור ל-OneCLI — ענן/דרך שמאפשרת לחבר את הסוכן למערכות וממשקים נוספים בקלות.\"\n167\t- **Reorder the library: WhatsApp BEFORE OneCLI.** WhatsApp is the most-wanted/common connection AND it pairs directly with the agent via QR (does NOT go through the OneCLI vault), so leading with it works and isn't blocked. OneCLI follows as the foundational vault for the OAuth services.\n168\t- New rail order under \"חיבורים נוספים\": WhatsApp → OneCLI (explained) → Gmail → Google Calendar → מילון.\n169\t- Consistency note: the OneCLI-FIRST verdict (#1912) was about the SEQUENCE WITHIN an OAuth connect (vault sign-in before the service screen), NOT the order of guides in the list. WhatsApp is vault-exempt, so listing it first is consistent.\n170\t\n171\t## CROSS-CUTTING PRINCIPLE: maximize AUTHENTICITY = \"this is MY personal guide\" (#2278) [BIG]\n172\t- Elia LOVES that the shots show his PERSONAL Telegram (his name visible) — explicitly keep it personal: \"אפילו שרואים את השם שלי והכל, זה ממש סבבה. אני משאיר את זה פרסונלי.\"\n173\t- THE GUIDING PRINCIPLE for the whole UI/design: **as REAL as possible, as much as possible MY screenshots, where you see MY screen.** Even the computer-screenshot top bar always shows the window/account label **\"אליה עבודה\"** — he LOVES that, KEEP it (do NOT crop/anonymize it).\n174\t- WHY: the more it looks like something HE personally prepared, the more it connects → reads as a PERSONAL guide, not a generic one. This is a feature, not a leak. (Consistent with his #2118 authorization to show his own name/emails.)\n175\t- Action: across all screens favor his authentic captures with his identity visible (Telegram name, \"אליה עבודה\" window title, his real desktop) over sanitized mocks. Apply this as the default design stance going forward. IRON-RULE still holds: live tokens/keys/passwords/pairing-codes stay redacted — personal identity is fine, live SECRETS are not.\n176\t\n177\t## Screen: Step 8 onboarding — show a few REAL onboarding examples (#2278)\n178\t- For the onboarding step (the agent's self-tour with Elia): show a FEW authentic examples of the onboarding it did with him — convey \"it does onboarding with me, prepares me.\" Say it's ~6 steps but DON'T show all six; show real example bubbles + the final (6th) message that \"you're ready to go / אפשר לצאת לדרך.\" Can describe the rest in words. Use his authentic Joni onboarding shots.\n179\t\n180\t## Screen: Telegram shots — use the REAL Telegram background, not black (#2276)\n181\t- Ref: attachment-1781597892884.jpg (the real Joni chat — authentic navy Telegram bg).\n182\t- Elia: every Telegram screenshot should sit on the AUTHENTIC Telegram chat background (navy/blue Telegram theme), NOT flattened on a black bg like I did on some. Rationale: the terminal shots look like a real terminal; the Telegram shots should look like real Telegram — each environment is recognizable. Right now everything is \"black on black\" → feels like one long threatening terminal. Real Telegram bg = less intimidating, signals \"now we're in Telegram, not the terminal.\"\n183\t- Action: audit ALL Telegram frames. Authentic captures already carry the real bg → keep. Any MOCK Telegram frames I built on pure black (e.g. botfather/pairing/start mocks) → REBUILD on the true Telegram chat background (navy theme, real bubble styling) so they match the authentic ones. Same principle per-environment: terminal=terminal chrome, Telegram=Telegram chrome, browser=browser chrome. Hand to builder/shots.\n184\t\n185\t## Screen: Step 6 Telegram — make the app DOWNLOAD clickable (#2266)\n186\t- Ref: attachment-1781597169223.jpg (step 6, micro mentions \"אפליקציית טלגרם בטלפון או במחשב\").\n187\t- Elia: give a clickable DOWNLOAD link/direction for the Telegram app — phone AND desktop — because some people don't have it installed. Good guide practice to point them to the download.\n188\t- Action: linkify \"טלגרם בטלפון\" → app store links (iOS App Store / Google Play) and \"במחשב/דסקטופ\" → https://desktop.telegram.org. (Round-4 already added a desktop.telegram.org link; extend to a clear \"להורדת טלגרם\" affordance covering phone + desktop, clickable.)\n189\t\n190\t## GLOBAL: DE-BOX the \"מה קורה כאן\" intro (#2262, #2264)\n191\t- Elia's design instinct: the two intro paragraphs sit inside a heavy bordered card (the .what box) that looks like a checkbox/container around what is essentially just a heading + subheading with a ✦. Feels redundant (\"מרגיש לי שהוא מיותר\"). He's consulting, flows with my call; also said keep it as-is and NOT a big subheading.\n192\t- DECISION (agreed): REMOVE the card border/bg from \"מה קורה כאן\" → render as a clean small teal EYEBROW label (15px/800 uppercase-ish) + plain 20px body text, no box. Keep \"מה קורה כאן\" SMALL (an eyebrow), not a large subheading.\n193\t- Principle: reserve boxed/bordered treatment ONLY for elements that must POP — 💡 tip, 🔴 \"נתקעת?\", 📋 copy blocks, 📷 screenshots. Over-boxing flattens hierarchy (when everything is a box, nothing stands out). Done in sample v3; the 💡 tip is now the only boxed block on the screen → it pops.\n194\t\n195\t## GLOBAL: BREADCRUMB must be GRANULAR per-step, not per-phase (#2248)\n196\t- Ref: attachment-1781596533255.jpg (step 4 top: crumb shows \"התקנה / התקנה\" = just the phase, duplicated/vague).\n197\t- Elia: the top חיווי should reflect EXACTLY which STEP he's on, not the phase bucket. \"אני בשלב 4, תסתכל למעלה, אני רואה שרק יש פה דבר אחד\" — feels imprecise; he wants every step/marker/bullet to pin his current location so he FEELS he's advancing a step.\n198\t- Action: change crumbs from `phase / phase` → `phase / שלב N · <step title>` (the current step named explicitly + highlighted). Done in the sample: \"הכנה / שלב 2 · איפה הסוכן יחיה?\". Apply globally — crumb's `.cur` = the live step name. Keeps the sense of forward motion at every step.\n199\t\n200\t## RAIL phase headers STILL too small + universal language (#2250)\n201\t- Feedback on the type sample: sizes look better overall, BUT the rail phase titles (הכנה/התקנה/חיבור/הפעלה) are still too small → enlarge. Done: 16px → **19px/800 teal** in sample.\n202\t- Use more universal/everyman LANGUAGE in the section titles (think \"שפה של כולם\").\n203\t- DEFER creative/visual flourish for the headers (\"טיפה יותר ברורות\" creative) to LATER — do NOT get stuck on creative now. For NOW: build it right, slightly enlarge fonts, get the type play correct + pleasant to read. Creative refinement = a later pass.\n204\t\n205\t## Screen: Step 4 \"מפתח ה-AI שלך\" (Anthropic) — ADD THE REAL SCREENSHOTS (#2252)\n206\t- Ref: attachment-1781596691359.jpg (step 4, 5 micro-steps, currently ALL text, NO screenshots).\n207\t- Elia: screenshots are MISSING here and it's \"מאוד מאוד חשוב\" — they give confidence (\"תחושת ביטחון\"). He will CAPTURE the Anthropic screens himself and send them. If any relevant shot is missing he'll shoot it at the end — but he wants ALL relevant screenshots present.\n208\t- Action: this is the gated Anthropic console flow (currently anthropic-1-login.png only; 5 `shot:'pending'`). Wire real shot slots for each micro: (1) console.anthropic.com login/\"Build with the Claude API\", (2) Continue-with-Google + Dashboard, (3) Billing → Add to credit balance ($5), (4) API Keys → Create Key → sk-ant dialog