{"parentUuid":"07b3066a-814f-40fe-9cf5-bf15c32278e5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/workspace/inbox/a2a-1781626627527-n3xv5g/GUIDE_INTEGRATION_round7_brief.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/inbox/a2a-1781626627527-n3xv5g/GUIDE_INTEGRATION_round7_brief.md","content":"# Guide Integration — Round 7 (the BIG morning-דגשים integration into index.html)\n\n**Why this exists:** all of Jun 16 morning was a screen-by-screen design review with Elia. Every note\nwas collected into specs + proven on SEPARATE live demo pages (opening-demo.html, rail-demo.html,\ntype sample). NONE of it was ever built into the actual guide engine `index.html` — it's still Round-6\n(mtime 06:34, before the review). Elia opened the live guide and saw zero of the changes. This round\nlands ALL of it into index.html in one pass.\n\nbuilder = sole editor of index.html. Do this as ONE coherent rebuild, then QA (402px + desktop, HE+EN\nparity, 0 em-dash). Return index.html + QA report → Daniela reviews + deploys.\n\n## Source-of-truth files (sent with this brief)\n- `index.html` — the engine to edit (Round-6 canonical).\n- `internal_screens_review_jun16.md` — THE master spec. Every screen note #2220-#2358. Authoritative.\n- `TYPE_SPEC_guide.md` — the formal type scale (approved). Introduce CSS vars --fs-h1..--fs-tip.\n- `rail-demo.html` — the APPROVED new side menu (rail) — structure/order/sizing to replicate in-engine.\n- `_type_sample.html` — the APPROVED type proof (step-2 sample) — match its proportions.\n\n## Build checklist (all from internal_screens_review_jun16.md — read it fully, this is the index)\n\n### GLOBAL\n1. **TYPE SCALE** — apply TYPE_SPEC_guide.md everywhere. No tiny text. Body 20/1.78, tips ≥18 prominent,\n   stuck/ok hints 17 white (not gray-13), H1 48, ladder 48→24→20→18→17. Mobile clamps, floor 15px. (#2234/#2238)\n   NOTE: rail **phase headers = 19/800 teal** (TYPE_SPEC has a stale 16 in one row — 19 is correct, #2250).\n   TIME claim: use ONE number consistently (the old micro still says 30–45; Elia floated 30–40 and 30–50).\n   Daniela will confirm the final number — until then leave a single token, do not mix.\n2. **REMOVE status/owner chips** (\"● מוכן\" / \"👤 אתה עושה\") from every step head. (#2268)\n3. **Step head structure** = H1 → teal lead one-liner (subtitle, NEW) → de-boxed \"מה קורה כאן\" eyebrow →\n   tip. Trim duplicate body paragraph. (#2268)\n4. **DE-BOX \"מה קורה כאן\"** → small teal eyebrow label (15/800) + plain 20px body, no card border.\n   Reserve boxes ONLY for: tip, \"נתקעת?\", copy blocks, screenshots. (#2262/#2264)\n5. **BREADCRUMB granular** → `phase / שלב N · <step title>`, current step named + highlighted. (#2248)\n6. **BOTTOM NAV** — prev/next at the bottom of every step too (keep top back). (#2290/#2292)\n7. **COPY BLOCKS** — every fixed/generic typed value → one-tap copy block (root, install one-liner,\n   claude, diagnostic prompt, chmod, /exit, BotFather cmds, agent name). EXCEPTION: user's own secrets\n   (root pw, their bot token, pairing code) stay manual. (#2244)\n8. **EMOJI policy = NONE** in titles/headings/prose. Replace legend/markers (🔵🔗📷🔴) + 💡 with clean\n   on-brand glyphs/dots/SVG + word \"טיפ\" with teal bar. (#2270) KEEP the \"✦ זה נשמע טכני אבל זה רק\n   העתק-הדבק\" reassurance line on command steps.\n9. **NanoClaw glossary** — add glossary term `nanoclaw` (open source / community / always-improving /\n   free). Linkify EVERY occurrence of \"NanoClaw\" in body → glossary popover (not just first). (#2220 #2258)\n9b. **NanoClaw community links-OUT block** (Elia's \"most important recommendation\", #2258) — a discreet\n   give-back block on step 1 near the NanoClaw callout: links out to NanoClaw's **Discord community,\n   GitHub repo/codebase, and website**. Use placeholder hrefs `#` for now — Daniela owes the real URLs\n   (pending from Elia). Build the block; leave the 3 hrefs as TODO. Do NOT drop this — it's separate from\n   the glossary linkify above.\n9c. **Personal-voice narrative (specific, #2232)** — weave Elia's exact \"I keep improving this\" line as\n   one of the tasteful personal touch-points (around the step-1 opener / strip): \"כשאני אראה שבאמת יש\n   עניין, אני אתקן ואשפר את המדריך ואכין לכם את זה שוב. אני אעדכן כל הזמן, תישארו מעודכנים.\" Ties to the\n   soft-register weekly-update thread.\n10. **Naming:** brand/guide = \"NanoShellano שלנו\"; personal agent moments (steps 7-8) = \"שלך\". All\n    brand/product names Latin in HE+EN (NanoClaw, not ננוקלו). (#2274/#2326)\n\n### RAIL (side menu) — replicate rail-demo.html in-engine (#2308-#2328)\n- Phase headers teal 19/800 (הכנה/התקנה/חיבור/הפעלה). Numbered circle dots (done/active/future). No emoji.\n- Step titles: 7 → \"תגיד שלום לננוקלו\"; 8 → \"היכרות עם הסוכן שלך\".\n- \"חיבורים נוספים\" section: WhatsApp → OneCLI (de-transliterated, labeled by what it does) → Gmail →\n  Google Calendar. (WhatsApp may later move up to chat-step; keep here for now per #2286.)\n- Bottom \"רוצה שאכין עוד מדריך?\" card — invite+register (name+email) ALWAYS visible; connection picker\n  behind a toggle (categorized OneCLI-verified scroll list, ~43, sticky teal category headers). Submit\n  wiring = leads backend (pending) — build UI now, leave submit stub. (#2328)\n- מילון = clean teal book SVG, no 📖.\n- RTL: rail on the RIGHT. Tight spacing — whole menu fits one screen.\n\n### PER-SCREEN\n- **Step 1 main:** add a מקרא/LEGEND card (4 marker rows: copy=blue/code, link, screenshot, red=stuck) +\n  one nav line (right rail = steps, bottom = connections). Concise. Personal first-person voice woven in\n  lightly (\"ככה אני מוביל אתכם / אני איתכם לאורך כל הדרך\"). Weave non-technical + time reassurance into\n  the step-1 opener. (#2228/#2230/#2226)\n- **Step 1 micro-3** chat-app line: connects to Telegram/WhatsApp/Slack+; in this guide we use Telegram\n  + WhatsApp. Keep short. (#2224)\n- **Step 2** → practical server-landscape page: compact provider rows (name + one-line + rough $/mo +\n  link), DigitalOcean tagged \"הכי נפוץ — נתחיל ממנו\", plan requirement (≥4GB RAM, not Google Cloud). (#2234)\n- **Step 3** → start DIRECTLY on DigitalOcean (no re-intro of providers); note \"process is the same on\n  every provider\". REMOVE the trailing bottom \"open provider\" CTA card; the link belongs at the TOP of\n  the step. Generalize: remove every end-of-page repeat \"open X\" button. (#2240/#2246/#2256)\n- **Step 4** (Anthropic): wire 5 real shot slots (login → dashboard → billing/credit → create-key →\n  saved). Elia supplies captures; leave shot:'pending' slots ready. Remove bottom redundant CTA. IRON:\n  never show a live sk-ant key. (#2252)\n- **Step 6 Telegram:** clickable \"להורדת טלגרם\" (iOS/Play + desktop.telegram.org). (#2266)\n- **Step 7** title → \"תגיד שלום לננוקלו שלך\". **Step 8** title → \"היכרות עם הסוכן שלך\". (#2270/#2274)\n- **Step 8 onboarding:** show a few REAL Joni onboarding example bubbles + the final \"אפשר לצאת לדרך\";\n  don't show all 6. (#2278)\n- **OneCLI step:** de-fragment to ONE crisp value paragraph (the vault; one connection → interface with\n  every API app, securely, revocable). Title \"OneCLI: הכספת שלך\". (#2288/#2286)\n- **DE-FRAGMENT is a GLOBAL rule, not OneCLI-only (#2288/#2294):** wherever several blocks on one screen\n  paraphrase the same point, MERGE into one. Apply to the **WhatsApp screen too** (it has the same\n  repeating \"לפני שמתחילים\" + \"מה קורה כאן\" fragmentation). Audit every screen for this disease.\n- **Telegram shots:** authentic navy Telegram bg, not black. Rebuild any black-bg mock TG frames. (#2276)\n- **Connection guides:** app logo/icon in each header (Calendar/Gmail/WhatsApp). Non-blocking nicety. (#2296)\n- **WhatsApp** is a chat CHANNEL: core step 6 = pick channel (Telegram default OR WhatsApp); WhatsApp\n  leaves the bottom \"חיבורים נוספים\" list. WhatsApp shots = needs-capture placeholder. (#2294)\n- **Shots hardening:** drop loading=\"lazy\" on in-flow shots (eager); don't let onerror permanently hide\n  a real existing shot — reserve graceful-hide only for shot:null/'pending'. (#2296→#2298)\n\n### ENTRY FLOW (NEW — #2468)\n- The new opening screen (opening-demo.html) becomes the real ENTRY. The old manifesto cover at the\n  index.html root is redundant and is being removed from flow; opening screen connects straight into the\n  guide. (Daniela handles wiring opening→guide; builder: make sure the guide's own topbar/menu match the\n  new direction so the transition is seamless. Elia will send final manifesto copy to place on the\n  opening page — separate.)\n\n## Constraints\n- 0 em-dashes (en-dash – in numeric ranges OK). No emoji. Brand names Latin.\n- Don't invent glossary terms with no data; flag missing ones.\n- Gated 3rd-party shots = needs-live-capture placeholders, never faked.\n- IRON-RULE: never embed live tokens/keys/passwords/pairing-codes.\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}},"displayPath":"../inbox/a2a-1781626627527-n3xv5g/GUIDE_INTEGRATION_round7_brief.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e7c89d2e-e7d0-4f9f-bd59-c6c5daa4f18e","timestamp":"2026-06-16T16:31:37.104Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"b522cebd-0184-435d-9a0b-60eb7d0a73fa","version":"2.1.154","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"breezy-launching-scott"}
