n build work so Daniela can manage rather than execute:\n- **Integrate content** into the engine. Daniela hands you a filled content brief (a JS data object in the project schema); you slot it into `index.html` as a guide, faithfully, word-for-word.\n- **QA** every change: render at 402px phone width (Playwright headless), check Hebrew RTL + English both, run integrity sweeps (0 em-dashes `—`; he+en parity — every text field has both; all screenshot paths resolve; no leftover `pending`/`status` placeholders; no real tokens/PII).\n- **Capture screenshots** of the guide's own UI via Playwright (element screenshots, `scale:'css'`). NOTE: you cannot capture gated third-party screens (Google/WhatsApp/etc. login & OAuth) — those need a live human run; flag them to Daniela as \"needs live capture\" rather than faking them.\n- **Report back** publish-ready artifacts (the updated `index.html` + any screenshot files) to Daniela. **You do NOT deploy** — Daniela holds the Vercel token and does the final deploy + talks to Elia.\n\n## The single-editor rule (critical — prevents drift)\nYou are the **sole editor of the engine** (`index.html`). One editor = no design drift. Daniela reviews and deploys; she does not edit the engine in parallel. Always work from the latest `index.html` Daniela sends you and send the full updated file back.\n\n## Iron rules (the project standard — never break)\n- Every text field is `{en:'...', he:'...'}`. Both required, never an empty `en`.\n- **0 em-dashes (—).** Use comma/period. (Numeric en-dash ranges like `5–12$` are fine and stay.)\n- Allowed inline HTML: `<b>` (buttons/names), `<code>` (commands/URLs), `<i>` (soft emphasis); `⚠️` allowed for warnings.\n- **Never a real token, key, phone number, email, name, OAuth code, or live QR — in text OR screenshots.** Dummy/blurred only. A live code = whoever uses it enters the account.\n- Tone: simple, \"talking to you,\" no jargon. Same voice as the install guide.\n- Hebrew quotes inside `'...'` strings: escape with `\\'` or wrap in double quotes.\n\n## Workflow per guide\n1. Daniela sends: the latest `index.html`, the filled content object (schema), screenshot files (or \"needs live capture\" notes), and the brand/standard.\n2. You integrate, QA at phone width in both languages, run the integrity sweep, capture any guide-UI screenshots you can.\n3. You send Daniela: the updated `index.html`, new screenshot files, and a short QA report (what you checked, what passed, what still needs a live capture).\n4. Daniela deploys and closes the loop with Elia.\n\n## Reporting cadence\n- Short tasks: just report the result.\n- Long/multi-guide work: a brief milestone note at natural transitions, not play-by-play.\n- Always surface what you could NOT verify or capture, explicitly — never let a gap read as \"done.\"\n\nKeep a `CLAUDE.local.md` in your workspace tracking the engine's data model, the schema, the brand tokens, and the state of each guide in the library, so context accumulates across sessions.\n\n---\n\n## Engine state (as of 2026-06-16, round2-complete) — LIVE on nanoclawguide.vercel.app\n\n**Canonical file:** `/workspace/agent/guide.html`\n**Status:** Round-2 E1–E7 + adopt-fixes deployed 2026-06-16. `node --check` passes clean. In sync with prod.\n\n**LEADS_ENDPOINT (NEVER blank):** `https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbxCvaR-oCJUJdxj5OeEKM42Hc8QEL5E_mB52OVsMtEgj79LPDb5xM_UHmRpTRR6T0dN/exec`\n\n**Architecture:** Hub model. `?guide=<id>` routes to guide view. `?lang=<he|en>` toggles language. `?start=1` opens wizard. All in one file. Guides accessible via deep link only — not exposed in cover/nav.\n\n**Round 5 new views:** `landing` (default, replaces cover) → `register` (3-field gate) → `wizard` (existing). Body starts `dir=\"rtl\" data-view=\"landing\"`.\n\n**Round 5 new functions:** `renderLanding()`, `renderRegister()`, `startRegistration()`, `submitRegistration()`, `toLanding()`. `window.submitLead=async function(){}` stub — Daniela wires backend.\n\n**Key data structures:**\n- `STEPS[]` — install wizard (8 steps, step 8 = Onboarding added in round 4)\n- `GLOSSARY[]` — 21 terms\n- `CONNECTION_GUIDES[]` — 4 guides: onecli, whatsapp, gmail, gcal (vercel removed round 4)\n- `MASCOT_SVG`, `WORDMARK_SVG` — inline SVG constants for cover + finish\n- `UI{}` — i18n strings\n\n**Note fields per guide:** onecli: null, whatsapp: null, gmail: OneCLI-first note, gcal: note with easier-after-Gmail\n\n**he/en key parity:** 403/403 — gap 0 (round 6; new micros all have {en,he})\n\n**Guide schema:** `{id, icon, hero?, title, oneLiner, estTime, prereqs, what, micro:[{do, cmd?, shot, ok, stuck?}], done, note}`\n- `cmd` field: string or `{en,he}` object → renders clickable copy-block in both render() and renderGuide()\n\n**Integration approach (critical — use for all future edits):**\n- NEVER use the Edit tool for large JS sections — it corrupts apostrophe delimiters\n- Use a Node.js script with `rep(old, new, label)` helper and `process.exit(1)` on NOT FOUND\n- All JS edits: string `.replace()` with exact anchors verified by grep first\n- Watch for: curly apostrophes U+2019 in single-quoted JS strings (contractions inside `'...'`), curly double quotes U+201C/U+201D in guide text, `⇕` vs `↑↓` arrow chars\n- WhatsApp/gmail/gcal guides use JSON double-quote key style `\"id\":\"...\"` not JS style `id:\"...\"`\n- For fix scripts: use **double-quoted** JS strings (not template literals) when embedding `\\'` escapes — in template literals `\\\\` = `\\` but in double-quoted strings `\\\\` also = `\\`. Key: to get `\\''` in the file (escape + close), write `\\\\''+` in the double-quoted string. Template literal `\\\\'` also gives `\\'`. Always verify with `indexOf` before + after.\n- After any JS edit, extract `<script>` block to .js and run `node --check` to verify syntax before reporting done.\n\n---\n\n## Guide library state (round 6)\n\n| Guide | Text | Shot status | Publish-ready |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **onecli** | ✓ | 4 shots present | Yes |\n| **whatsapp** | ✓ | all 5 shots: needs live capture | No |\n| **gmail** | ✓ | 3 shots present | Yes |\n| **gcal** | ✓ | 3 shots present | Yes |\n\n## Wizard shot coverage (round 6)\n\n**45 authentic shots landed** (DO: 11, Anthropic: 3, Terminal: 14, Self-heal: 9, Telegram: 8).\n\n| File | Step | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `do-product.jpg` … `do-console-login.jpg` | Step 3 (10 micros) | DO account → console login |\n| `anthropic-dashboard.jpg` … `anthropic-createkey.jpg` | Step 4 (3 micros) | Anthropic billing → key |\n| `do-paste-cmd.jpg`, `term-flow-clean.jpg` … `term-cli-install.jpg` | Step 5 (14 micros) | Install sequence |\n| `tg-channel-menu.jpg` … `tg-ready.jpg` | Step 6 (4 micros) | Telegram setup |\n| `tg-empty-start.jpg`, `tg-hello.jpg`, `sh-diagnose.jpg` … `sh-delivered.jpg` | Step 7 (11 micros) | Hello + 9-frame self-heal |\n| `tg-onboard.jpg` | Step 8 | Onboarding |\n\nPre-round-6 shots still present: `onecli-*.jpg`, `google-*.jpg`, `nanoshellanoo.png`.\n\n## Shots in `/workspace/agent/shots/`\n\n`nanoshellanoo.png` — Mascot hero. Must be RGBA colorType-6 transparent PNG. Ping Daniela before integrating any new version.\n\n## Open flags\n\n### Live state (nanoclawguide.vercel.app, 2026-06-16)\n- `window.submitLead` stays stub until Elia picks datastore (A: Vercel Postgres / B: Google Sheet) — Daniela owns wire-in\n- Round 5 open polish (low priority): faint teal radial glow behind mascot on landing\n\n### Still missing shots (needs live capture by Elia)\n- `shots/term-5-set.png` — Step 5 micro[19], installer \"You're set\" completion screen (caught by onerror, no visible break)\n- whatsapp: all 5 shots\n- gmail: gmail-1-ask.png, gmail-3-notverified.png, gmail-6-test.png\n- gcal: gcal-1-ask.png, gcal-3-notverified.png, gcal-6-event.png\n\n### Notes\n- Playwright + Chromium installed at `/workspace/agent/.playwright/`. QA scripts: `qa-guides.js`, `qa-full.js`, `qa-round6.js`\n- Transform methodology: use Node.js `.mjs` scripts with `rep(old,new,label)` + `process.exit(1)` on NOT FOUND. Never use Edit tool for large JS sections.\n- Daniela added `.vercelignore` for `shots/onecli-raw`, `shots/*.html`, `brand-mock.html`\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":11,"newStart":33,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","-## Engine state (as of 2026-06-16, round2-complete) — LIVE on nanoclawguide.vercel.app","+## Engine state (as of 2026-06-16, round3-complete) — LIVE on nanoclawguide.vercel.app"," "," **Canonical file:** `/workspace/agent/guide.html`","-**Status:** Round-2 E1–E7 + adopt-fixes deployed 2026-06-16. `node --check` passes clean. In sync with prod.","+**Status:** Round-3 deployed 2026-06-16 (dpl_5j8zWSPb92xqdToa8jdy5mn67yzU). In sync with prod."," ","+**Round-3 changes (canonical):**","+- STEPS[1] now has full `compare:{}` block (4 providers + ⚠️ 4GB req + no Google Cloud). STEPS[2] is action-first, no compare.","+- All `$5–12` / `5–12$` price strings → `$24` / `~24$` (6 occurrences across micros + note)","+- Finish screen: `section#finish` stays standalone OUTSIDE `.shell` (full-width page, no rail). Elia reverted rail decision (#2738). `showDone()` has NO `render()` call.","+- `tg-token-prompt-strip.jpg` in step 6 slot (was full frame)","+- Language toggle: עב/EN (unified across pages)","+"," **LEADS_ENDPOINT (NEVER blank):** `https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbxCvaR-oCJUJdxj5OeEKM42Hc8QEL5E_mB52OVsMtEgj79LPDb5xM_UHmRpTRR6T0dN/exec`"," "," **Architecture:** Hub model. `?guide=<id>` routes to guide view. `?lang=<he|en>` toggles language. `?start=1` opens wizard. All in one file. Guides accessible via deep link only — not exposed in cover/nav."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"04102eca-3953-4a84-8b30-e040a54f88de","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"b522cebd-0184-435d-9a0b-60eb7d0a73fa","version":"2.1.154","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"breezy-launching-scott"}
